WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.374 --> 00:00:02.127
Your bank says the money has left.

2
00:00:02.555 --> 00:00:04.488
The receiver says nothing arrived.

3
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.513
So where exactly did your money go?

4
00:00:07.165 --> 00:00:08.838
Here's what most people don't realise.

5
00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.688
A bank transfer isn't money jumping between phones.

6
00:00:12.074 --> 00:00:15.104
An entire payment system works behind that notification.

7
00:00:15.745 --> 00:00:17.553
When you send to another Nigerian bank,

8
00:00:17.656 --> 00:00:19.616
your bank initiates the transfer.

9
00:00:20.017 --> 00:00:23.044
The message moves through Nigeria's interbank payment infrastructure,

10
00:00:23.196 --> 00:00:26.096
including NIBSS Instant Payment, to the receiving bank.

11
00:00:26.717 --> 00:00:27.640
But here's the twist.

12
00:00:28.707 --> 00:00:32.490
A timeout, delayed response or unresolved status can leave both sides

13
00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.270
with different information. Your account may show a debit,

14
00:00:35.378 --> 00:00:38.175
while the receiver's account is not yet confirmed as credited.

15
00:00:38.831 --> 00:00:40.827
And sometimes the money actually arrived.

16
00:00:41.231 --> 00:00:42.880
But the SMS alert was delayed,

17
00:00:43.018 --> 00:00:45.810
or never came. That's why an alert alone isn't enough.

18
00:00:46.231 --> 00:00:48.300
Check the balance and transaction history.

19
00:00:48.958 --> 00:00:49.688
So what should you do?

20
00:00:50.949 --> 00:00:51.906
Don't send the money again.

21
00:00:52.941 --> 00:00:55.241
Save your receipt and transaction session ID.

22
00:00:55.642 --> 00:01:00.330
In Nigeria, NIBSS provides a NIP tracker through star five-six-five star five

23
00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:03.086
hash, for eligible transfers within 48 hours.

24
00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:06.155
If it's successful, the receiver should ask their bank to trace

25
00:01:06.235 --> 00:01:08.929
it. If not, contact your bank about the reversal.

26
00:01:09.571 --> 00:01:11.703
And if your bank doesn't resolve it, escalate.

27
00:01:12.119 --> 00:01:13.262
Complain to your bank first.

28
00:01:14.111 --> 00:01:16.742
If unresolved within the applicable two-week period,

29
00:01:16.848 --> 00:01:19.660
escalate to the CBN's Consumer Protection Department.

30
00:01:20.309 --> 00:01:23.591
So next time a transfer says successful but nothing arrives,

31
00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:25.215
don't just ask where the money went.

32
00:01:25.631 --> 00:01:27.037
Ask for the transaction trail.
